# Model Check: Restating the Data Model

A **track** is one sequential line of work; steps in the same track never overlap, and anything that happens while something else happens belongs in a different track. A **step** has exactly one duration kind: `fixed` (a number of seconds), `variable` (a range with min, max, and default), or `indefinite` (runs until the person stops it). A **startTrigger** ties a step to the clock or to another step—`programStart` (at t=0), `programStartOffset` (at a specific offset), `afterStep` (when another step ends, optionally with an offset), `afterStepWithBuffer` (when another step ends plus a buffer), `manual` (user taps to start), `onAbort` (only if another step is aborted), or `compound` (wait for all or the first of several triggers). **stepId**s are unique across the WHOLE program, not per track, so no two steps anywhere can have the same name. Every `task` a step occupies needs a matching `resourceConstraints` entry, and that entry's `maxConcurrent` is what stops two steps from sharing one oven, one thermocycler, or one PA at the same time. Work repeated n times (n trays, n samples, n aircraft) is declared as `replicates: {count: n, mode: "serial" | "parallel" | "stagger"}` on ONE step—never n hand-copied steps or tracks—and what follows each repetition chains with `{"type":"afterStep","stepId":"<step>","instances":"each"}`, the step that waits for all instances uses `{"instances":"all"}`, and when the holding area between them only fits k at a time (a rack holding two trays, a rotor holding six tubes) set `replicates.maxInFlight: k` so the upstream step is held back instead of stranding the downstream one.

```json
{
  "acknowledgement": "tracks are sequential lines of work; one duration kind per step; triggers link steps; every task needs a resourceConstraint; stepIds are global",
  "resourceConstraints": [
    { "task": "oven", "maxConcurrent": 1 },
    { "task": "burner", "maxConcurrent": 4 },
    { "task": "prep", "maxConcurrent": 2 }
  ],
  "actors": 2
}
```
